{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-10T12:54:03.603Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e64a4bf384d39392d902ceda","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1699","claim:pm-nhauur","lineage:pm-nhauur","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1699+pm-nhauur","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1699","claim:pm-nhauur","lineage:pm-nhauur","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.322","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-5htunt"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Telemetry and Sentry scrubbers keep URL credentials whose host has no dot: attempted_args ships https://token@localhost and user:password@registry:8080 verbatim"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-10 while fixing pm-nhauur. Telemetry redaction of command arguments (sanitizeString/sanitizeCommandArgs in src/core/telemetry/runtime.ts) relies on redactEmailTokens, and Sentry's scrubString (src/core/sentry/instrument.ts) on an email regex that needs a dotted TLD. URL userinfo is only removed when it happens to look like an email address. Reproduced with the built CLI, an isolated PM_GLOBAL_PATH and PM_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT pointed at an unreachable local port so events stay queued: 'pm package install https://tok3nSecret@localhost/x.tgz --bogus-flag' and 'pm package install https://u:p!ss-Secret9@registry:8080/x.tgz --bogus-flag' both queue a command_error event whose attempted_args contain the token and the password tail verbatim. A single-label host, a host:port, an IP literal or a password with a character outside the email local-part set defeats the heuristic. redactUrlsInText (GH-1660) only runs on error messages and only for scheme:// spellings. Fix: one conservative token rule shared with the CLI refusal path (pm-nhauur) — any token with a ':' before its last '@' has the span between them replaced — applied to every telemetry argument before the existing sanitizers and to every whitespace-delimited word of free text in both scrubbers. Duplicate check: searched 'telemetry url credentials attempted_args', 'GH-1660 redact urls telemetry'; pm-nhauur covers CLI stdout/stderr only."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["privacy","redaction","security","sentry","telemetry"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-10T12:54:03.603Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-10T12:54:03.603Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Telemetry attempted_args, attempted command and free-text fields remove the span between a token's first ':' and last '@' (keeping scheme slashes) before every other sanitizer, at both capture levels; Sentry scrubString applies the same rule to every whitespace-delimited word; Specs cover a single-label host, host:port, token-only userinfo, a password with characters outside the email local-part set, and a backslash authority; the existing diagnostic-privacy and telemetry redaction suites stay green"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5oj5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"No telemetry event or Sentry payload carries URL userinfo for any token whose ':' precedes its last '@', whatever the host shape."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-nhauur","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-10T12:54:03.603Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"dbf1be6c749754fa61e6b3af10fccad4f1c77387122cca54c81ab6e8a418d139","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"05aa1d966b1554654c75e6dfbcc3a59fbc154ae062b7fa92e7a256981b27cccb"}
